Let $\theta=\angle AOB$. Since a tangent is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact, $\angle OAC=90^\circ$.

$$\begin{align*}
\tan\theta&=\frac{AC}{OA}\\
\tan\theta&=\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\\
\theta&=\frac{\pi}{6}
\end{align*}$$

$$\begin{align*}
L&=r\theta\\
L&=\sqrt{3}\times\frac{\pi}{6}\\
L&=\frac{\pi\sqrt{3}}{6}
\end{align*}$$
